    "id": "evt_columbia_classics_863b3403d6",
    "name": "Classics Lecture Series Presents: Ioanna Karamanou (Aristotle University of Thessaloniki)",
    "description": "Tuesday, April 29, 2025 4:10 PM 6:00 PM 16:10 18:00 Department of Classics at Columbia University in the City of New York (map) Google Calendar ICS The New Euripides Papyrus (P. Phil.. Nec. 23 v ):Fresh Perspectives on Tragic RhetoricAbstract:In November 2022, a team of archaeologists from the Egyptian mission at the necropolis of Philadelphia in Egypt unearthed from a tomb a papyrus that contained 97 (to a considerable extent otherwise unattested) lines of Euripides’ fragmentarily preserved tragedies Ino and Polyidos. The papyrus was edited (in ZPE 230 [2024] 1-40) by Prof. John Gibert and Assistant Prof. Yvona Trnka Amrhein (University of Colorado Boulder), who launched a project towards interpreting this amazing new finding.The present lecture, which derives from this project, will seek to explore thedebate (agon) in Euripides’ Polyidos preserved in 60 lines of this new papyrus text. It will investigate the structure of this debate, which takes place between King Minos and the se...",
