    "name": "Classics Lecture Series Presents: Luke Lea (Columbia University)",
    "description": "Friday, December 6, 2024 4:10 PM 6:00 PM 16:10 18:00 Department of Classics at Columbia University in the City of New York (map) Google Calendar ICS Hello everyone,We are excited to invite you to the fourth and last talk of the Fall 2024 Semester!Luke Lea (Columbia University) will give his talk entitled Good “Because of Itself” in Republic II. The talk will occur on Friday, December 6th, at 4:10 p.m. EDT in Hamilton 603 and on Zoom. A reception will follow. If you would like to receive a Zoom link, please email Holly Axford (ha2694@columbia.edu). The Zoom link will be circulated the day before the talk. Our speaker has kindly agreed to precirculate an abstract, pasted below. A poster for the event is also attached to the bottom of this email.We hope to see you all there!All the best,Holly Axford, Gia Chen, Paraskevi Martzavou, Umberto Verdura, and Gareth WilliamsColumbia Classics Lectures Series Co-Organizers**************************************************************************...",
