    "id": "evt_columbia_1c4a8c0b",
    "name": "Le Corbeau -- Censored Film Series",
    "description": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Le Corbeau (The Raven)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt; Henri-Georges Clouzot, 1943, 92 min.&lt;br /&gt; In French with English subtitles&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt; Discussion with Nicholas Elliott and Shanny Peer&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Register &lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/screening-of-le-corbeau-the-raven-tickets-1389498650869?aff=oddtdtcreator\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;A wave of anonymous poison-pen letters signed &amp;ldquo;Le Corbeau&amp;rdquo; (&amp;ldquo;The Raven&amp;rdquo;) unsettles a quiet provincial town, gradually revealing the paranoia, resentment, and moral decay lurking beneath its tranquil fa&amp;ccedil;ade. Henri-Georges Clouzot&amp;rsquo;s &lt;em&gt;Le Corbeau &lt;/em&gt;(1943) is a chilling psychological thriller and a razor-sharp allegory of authoritarianism, suspicion, and collective guilt.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Read more&lt;/p&gt;",
