    "description": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Catherine Cusset&lt;/strong&gt; in conversation with Elisabeth Ladenson&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;Register &lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/how-proust-and-hockney-can-lift-your-spirits-tickets-1425808825579?aff=oddtdtcreator\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;One has a reputation for being a difficult writer; the other is an easy painter, accessible to all. Catherine Cusset has devoted a novel to the British David Hockney and a personal essay to Marcel Proust. In their work she finds a life lesson, inspiration, comfort, irony, and a certainty: that art is a life saver, and that you should only write, or paint, what matters to you.&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Catherine Cusset&lt;/strong&gt; is an award-winning, bestselling author of 15 novels, including &lt;em&gt;Le probl&amp;egrave;me avec Jane&lt;/em&gt; (Grand Prix des lectrices d&amp;rsquo;Elle 2000); &lt;em&gt;Confessions d&amp;rsquo;une radine&lt;/em&gt;; &lt;em&gt;Un brillant avenir&lt;/em...",
