    "id": "evt_newschool_8a3ca026",
    "name": "Economics Seminar: Jamee Moudud",
    "description": "Dr. Moudud (PhD 1998) will present his new book “Legal and Political Foundations of Capitalism: the End of Laissez Faire?” The title is an extension of John R. Commons’ classic book “Legal Foundations of Capitalism” and an important article by John Maynard Keynes, “The End of Laissez Faire”. The question mark captures the essence of the book. Drawing on the insights of the Original Institutional Economics and American Legal Realist tradition along with those of Adam Smith, Karl Polanyi, and Piero Sraffa it provides new insights on the nature of institutions in capitalism. By arguing that society is a political community it challenges the private law versus public law or state versus markets distinction. Focusing on property, credit and public finance, constitutional law and social rights, monetary sovereignty and colonialism, corporations, and authoritarianism this book argues that laissez faire is the foundational myth of capitalism and that “state intervention versus de‑regulation...",
