    "id": "evt_newschool_905ae6cb",
    "name": "Economics Seminar: Naoki Yoshihara",
    "description": "Dr Yoshihara from UMASS/ Amherst, will present \"Sraffian Indeterminacy\".﻿Unlike the neoclassical school, the classical and Marxian schools view long-period equilibrium in a capitalist market economy as a system with one degree of freedom, as described by Piero Sraffa. However, neoclassical economists have criticized this vision, pointing out that Sraffa's system does not account for excess demand conditions in goods and factor markets. This presentation discusses recent research trends regarding Sraffian equilibrium indeterminacy that demonstrate the unfounded nature of neoclassical criticism. External guests, please register using the link, so that security at our building has your name, otherwise you will be denied entry. Thanks.",
