    "id": "evt_newschool_37e45d0b",
    "name": "Print Media and the Authoritarian Turn in India, China, and the United States",
    "description": "The panel features scholars and writers offering perspectives on print media and investigative journalism as a global authoritarian turn erodes norms of press freedom in India and the United States, and eliminates once acceptable forms of investigative practices in Chinese journalism. Under the authoritarian turn, states are using laws on libel and other statutes to sanction commercial print media outlets. Popular pressurefrom illiberal social organizations have also been used to intimidate and physically attack journalists, domestically and transnationally. Panelists will discuss recent research and writing projects on government efforts to restrict if not control what journalists and writers produce, as well as coping strategies they have deployed in response.",
