    "name": "Documentary Screening - The Life of Brian (Maguire): The New Film on an Irish Art Legend",
    "description": "The Life of Brian (Maguire) is a powerful new documentary that explores the extraordinary life and work of acclaimed Irish artist and social activist Brian Maguire. Directed by Mark McLoughlin, the film follows Maguire’s journey as he uses art to spotlight global injustices—from poverty and violence to the plight of migrants in the Arizona desert. Through his raw, politically charged work, Maguire gives voice to the marginalized and challenges dominant narratives. This special screening at NYU DC is presented in collaboration with Solas Nua and the Embassy of Ireland, and will feature a post-film Q&amp;A with Brian Maguire, director Mark McLoughlin, and producer Dara Jauch.",
